# Additional private Compose interpolation for the FOUR-file local stack:
# base + operations + stack + self-hosted.full-backup.compose.yml.
# This does not enable production browser/assets/public registration.
ODDPATH_FULL_BACKUP_ENV_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/full-backup.env
ODDPATH_FULL_BACKUP_STATE_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-full-backup-state
ODDPATH_FULL_BACKUP_ARCHIVE_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-full-archives
ODDPATH_FULL_VAULT_EXPORT_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-vault-export
ODDPATH_FULL_RUNTIME_EXPORT_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-runtime-export
ODDPATH_FULL_ESCROW_KEY_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/independent-escrow-key

# Reuse the stack's actual vault/runtime source volumes and private vault keyring.
# Do not change their permissions: vault UID1000/private0700, runtime UID0/private0700.
# Provision the NEW full-backup-state/archive/runtime-export volumes UID0/mode0700;
# provision the NEW vault-export volume UID1000/mode0700. Never reuse user volumes.
# The two exporters run as each source's native owner, with no network/keys/PG
# credentials/Docker socket. SQLite opens the source readOnly; its directory must
# allow the owner's normal WAL/SHM bookkeeping. Export snapshots use private tmpfs.
# The aggregator sees only their private Unix sockets; it has no live-journal mount.
# UID0 + DAC_READ_SEARCH reads private keys/socket paths, with group1000 for the
# vault socket. No DAC_OVERRIDE or Docker socket is granted to this backup service.
# Initialize truly NEW source journals using the existing owner/module bootstrap
# before selecting this profile. Missing source files fail readiness; never create
# an empty replacement for a lost/uncertain existing journal.
#
# ODDPATH_BACKUP_KEY_FILE and ODDPATH_BACKUP_PGPASS_FILE keep their existing meaning.
# The escrow key is a DIFFERENT random256-bit lowercase-hex key, mode0600, also
# different from every vault key. Escrow wraps the existing vault keyring under
# this separate key; neither archive contains either wrapping/master key.
# Keep both master keys separately protected and independently recoverable.
# Optionally escrow an explicit private JSON operator configuration using a
# separately reviewed read-only mount and ODDPATH_FULL_OPERATOR_ESCROW_FILE.
# External provider/SMTP/DB runtime credentials are not copied automatically.
#
# full-backup.env contains ONLY the dedicated SELECT-only source PG configuration:
# PGHOST=postgres
# PGPORT=5432
# PGDATABASE=oddpath
# PGUSER=oddpath_backup
# PGSSLMODE=disable
# If READY objects exist, add separately scoped GET-only credentials:
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<32-hex-account>.eu.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# R2_REGION=auto
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=<private-bucket>
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<read-only-id>
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<read-only-secret>
# Never add PGPASSWORD, DATABASE_URL, admin/migrator/recovery credentials or live
# API/provider secrets. Production object transport requires the exact EU HTTPS
# endpoint. The synthetic HTTP endpoint override is available only to local tests.
#
# Use ONLY --profile full-backup for this data, after validating all four files.
# Existing --profile backup stays CLOSED_DATABASE_ONLY and keeps refusing these
# records. Both use the existing supervisor/locking/failure-health machinery.
# Full backup uses a distinct job identity: an old DB-only success cannot make
# the full job healthy. Every unsuccessful create still terminates the supervisor
# container, so restart clears private decrypted tmpfs before another success.
#
# The daily full archive includes a consistent PG dump, on-demand supported SQLite
# exports and checksum-verified READY object bytes. Components are independent
# captures, not one atomic multi-store checkpoint. Non-READY records remain in PG
# and are counted as not yet durable; their pending upload bytes are not promised.
# Data and escrow have EXACTLY the same seven-day retention timestamp. Both are
# AEAD-encrypted and independently authenticated; copy both + their SHA256 receipts.
# Local files/copies are not proof of an off-host failure domain. offHostCopyVerified
# remains false until the separate actual off-host transfer/recovery gate passes.
#
# Recovery commands (new private recovery credentials/mounts, never source role):
# node ops/full-backup.mjs verify /archives/<data>.opb
# node ops/full-backup.mjs restore-keys /archives/<escrow>.opb --confirm-directory /private/new-keys
# node ops/full-backup.mjs restore /archives/<data>.opb --confirm-target oddpath_restore_<unique>
# For restore set ODDPATH_RESTORE_ACK=ISOLATED_EMPTY_TARGET and PGUSER/PGPASSFILE to
# an exclusive recovery owner on an empty, isolated target. The backup profile does
# NOT mount recovery credentials: supply a separate private recovery overlay.
# ODDPATH_FULL_RESTORE_DIRECTORY must be a NEW absolute path outside the checkout,
# in a private0700 parent. Archives can stay read-only; recovery receipts go there.
# Supply the exact escrowed keyring via ODDPATH_FULL_VAULT_KEYRING_FILE. Key rotation
# is explicit: never replace the deployment's current keys with old recovered keys.
# Optionally stage an independent source via ODDPATH_CURRENT_REVOCATIONS_SOCKET.
# Its MAC integrity does not prove it is the latest globally current source.
#
# Restored PG, objects and historical journals ALWAYS remain quarantined. No
# application starts, no grants are installed and no runtime/fence/hold is reset.
# Historical journals are under historical/, not mounted into live services.
# Any independent journal is under current/, with freshness still UNVERIFIED.
# Post-snapshot consumption/deletions need current independent evidence/PITR;
# missing evidence is never zero usage, a guessed debit or provider replay.
# Apply deletions/revocations, prove physical Stop/settlement, then obtain separate
# recovery/activation acceptance before any live import. A populated target or
# lost final acknowledgement requires inspection, never blind overwrite/retry.
# Remove the isolated drill database and decrypted private staging after the drill.
